/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 174 0 R
/T (India \(and globally\) is facing a rapidly aging population. By 2031, India will have approximately 19.4 crore elderly people \(aged 60+\), and over 70% of them live without continuous monitoring. Falls are the number one cause of injury-related deaths among the elderly, and in emergencies such as heart issues or breathing problems, even a small delay in detection can be fatal.)
/E (India \(and globally\) is facing a rapidly aging population. By 2031, India will have approximately 19.4 crore elderly people \(aged 60+\), and over 70% of them live without continuous monitoring. Falls are the number one cause of injury-related deaths among the elderly, and in emergencies such as heart issues or breathing problems, even a small delay in detection can be fatal.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [2]
>>
